# Generated Files

## Purpose

Prevent hand-editing of derived artifacts that a generator will overwrite.

## When Applied

Anything under `docs/generated/**` (and similar generated output).

## Requirements

- Treat `docs/generated/**` as build output — change the generator/source, then regenerate.
- Do not hand-edit generated files as if they were the source of truth.
- If a generated file is wrong, fix the upstream input and note it in [`documentation.mdc`](documentation.mdc).

## Examples

- Wrong entry in a generated index → fix the source doc/config, regenerate.

## Anti-patterns

- Editing a generated file directly to "fix" output.

## Common Mistakes

- Committing a hand-edit that the next generation run silently reverts.
